            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3(9^x)-7(6^x)+2(4^x)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nDivide by $4^x>0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}3\\left(\\frac94\\right)^x-7\\left(\\frac32\\right)^x+2&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nLet $u=(\\frac{3}{2})^x>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3u^2-7u+2&=0\\\\(3u-1)(u-2)&=0\\\\u&=\\frac13\\quad\\text{or}\\quad u=2.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values are positive.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac32\\right)^x&=\\frac13\\quad\\text{or}\\quad \\left(\\frac32\\right)^x=2\\\\x\\ln\\left(\\frac32\\right)&=-\\ln 3\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x\\ln\\left(\\frac32\\right)=\\ln 2\\\\x&=-\\frac{\\ln 3}{\\ln(3/2)}\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=\\frac{\\ln 2}{\\ln(3/2)}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
